cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GasBrineBench: a benchmark dataset of experimental gas-brine thermodynamic data"
abstract: >-
  A curated, quality-coded benchmark of experimental thermodynamic data for
  gas-brine systems: gas solubility, brine density, osmotic coefficients,
  vapor-pressure lowering, gas-phase water content, enthalpy of dissolution
  and brine permittivity, in single- and mixed-salt aqueous electrolyte
  solutions. 5,846 rows from 82 published sources, covering seven gases
  (CO2, CH4, H2, N2, O2, C2H6, C3H8) and six ions (Na+, K+, Ca2+, Mg2+, Cl-,
  SO4 2-) over 273-623 K and 0.1-3,500 bar. Every row carries its source, an
  R/T/U quality code with a documented justification, and a fit/test tag; the
  raw hand transcriptions the values were typed from are included.
message: >-
  The numerical values are measurements published by the authors cited in
  SOURCES.md; please cite those primary sources for the data you use, and
  this repository for the compilation. Pre-release: a Zenodo version DOI and
  a data-descriptor reference will be added at v1.0.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Moortgat
    given-names: Joachim
    affiliation: The Ohio State University
keywords:
  - gas solubility
  - brine
  - electrolyte
  - equation of state
  - carbon storage
  - benchmark dataset
